---
import AuditDiagram from "./AuditDiagram.astro";

// Bagian 5. Sumber angka: HASIL_UJICOBA_TAMBAHAN/README.md (25 Juli 2026) dan
// metrics_summary.json tiap folder hasil, sudah dicocokkan satu per satu.
//
// PENTING soal narasi. Perbaikan kebocoran 29% TIDAK menurunkan akurasi.
// Akurasi tetap 1,0000 setelah split dibersihkan. Yang menurunkannya ke
// 0,9606-0,9774 adalah ablasi resolusi. Jangan pernah menyandingkan angka
// 29% dengan 97,7% seolah yang satu menyebabkan yang lain. CV lama
// melakukan itu dan implikasinya keliru.
const pipeline = [
  {
    stage: "Qwen3-VL",
    role: "Semantic gate. Rejects anything that is not an ID card, zero-shot.",
    detail:
      "It has to throw out a photo of a desk, a hand, a blank wall, before any of that reaches the classifier. Evaluated separately with an LLM-as-a-judge pass over card and non-card images, where it scored perfectly.",
  },
  {
    stage: "Florence-2 + Canny",
    role: "Phrase grounding locates the card, then edge detection crops and deskews it.",
    detail:
      "Florence-2 says where the card is, Canny finds its edges, and the crop straightens it. The classifier never sees the desk it was lying on, so background stops being a feature it can cheat with.",
  },
  {
    stage: "EfficientNet-B0",
    role: "Binary classifier, genuine against forged.",
    detail:
      "Two-phase transfer learning from ImageNet: the head trains first with the backbone frozen, then the whole network fine-tunes. Mixup at alpha 0.4, AdamW, seed 42. The shipped model runs at 1024×474 and fits in 4 GB of VRAM.",
  },
  {
    stage: "Grad-CAM",
    role: "Heatmap over the region that drove the decision.",
    detail:
      "This is the part that keeps the rest honest. On a font forgery the heat sits on the text block; on a face swap it sits on the portrait. If it had lit up the background instead, the accuracy figure would have meant nothing.",
  },
];
---

<section class="section section--ink" id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
  <div class="shell">
    <span class="section__label">Projects</span>
    <h2 id="projects-title" class="rise">Two I can defend line by line</h2>

    <article class="project">
      <header class="role__head">
        <h3>Student ID card forgery detection</h3>
        <p class="figure role__meta">
          Final year project · PyTorch, FastAPI, Next.js 14, OpenCV ·
          <a
            class="figure--verified"
            href="https://github.com/Dwiyuda/KTM-Detector-UIR-Skripsi_Public"
            rel="noopener">Repository</a
          >
        </p>
      </header>

      <p class="measure project__lede">
        Card checks at the university library were a person looking at a card.
        The printed QR code was never wired to any database, so a good forgery
        only had to survive a glance. This is a four-stage pipeline that decides
        instead, and shows its reasoning.
      </p>

      {/* Akordeon eksklusif lewat atribut name, tanpa JavaScript. Peramban
          yang belum mendukungnya tetap bisa membuka tiap tahap, hanya bisa
          terbuka bersamaan. */}
      <ol class="pipeline rise-group">
        {
          pipeline.map((p, i) => (
            <li class="pipeline__step">
              <details name="ktm-pipeline" open={i === 0}>
                <summary>
                  <span class="pipeline__no figure">{`0${i + 1}`}</span>
                  <span class="pipeline__stage figure">{p.stage}</span>
                  <span class="pipeline__role">{p.role}</span>
                </summary>
                <p class="pipeline__detail">{p.detail}</p>
              </details>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>

      <p class="measure">
        The dataset is 1,645 images, 845 genuine scans and 800 forgeries built
        under five scenarios: generative-AI face swap, font inconsistency,
        print-scan recapture, identity text tampering, and hybrids that stack
        one on another. The model that ships runs at 1024×474 on a group-aware
        80:10:10 split and scores 1.0000 across accuracy, precision, recall,
        F1, and ROC-AUC. It fits in 4 GB of VRAM.
      </p>

      <div class="audit">
        <p class="audit__label figure">The audit</p>

        <div class="measure">
          <p>
            Four models. Four perfect scores, with confusion matrices holding no
            errors at all. A result like that is not something to celebrate. It
            is a reason to go and check the data.
          </p>

          <p>
            The check found something. Every forgery was built from a real card
            and kept its number, so <code>real_214</code> became
            <code>fake_214</code>. My split script shuffled the genuine files
            and the forged files independently, which let two halves of one
            physical card land on opposite sides of the train-test boundary. On
            the 80:10:10 split, <span class="audit__figure"
              >48 of 165 test images</span
            > were contaminated. That is 29.1%. On 70:15:15 it was 71 of 248.
          </p>
        </div>

        <AuditDiagram />

        <div class="measure audit__rest">
          <p class="audit__turn">Then I retrained, and it was still 1.0000.</p>

          <p>
            The leak was real and it explained nothing. I had spent the audit
            proving my own suspicion wrong. A five-fold group-aware
            cross-validation agreed. At 1024×474 the two classes genuinely do
            separate, and the contamination had been riding along without
            changing the outcome.
          </p>

          <p>
            My examiners raised a different objection. If every model scores
            1.0, there is no basis for saying which one is better. They asked
            for results that were not perfect.
          </p>

          <p>
            The quick way to do that is to make the numbers worse. I did not.
            Instead I ran a resolution ablation, holding every other parameter
            fixed and dropping the input to each architecture's native size,
            224×224 for B0 and 300×300 for B3. Accuracy fell to between
            <span class="figure">0.9606</span> and
            <span class="figure">0.9774</span> on its own, and the fall carried
            information: the model leans on high-frequency forensic traces that
            do not survive being shrunk.
          </p>

          <p>
            Every false negative in those runs came from one scenario. Font
            inconsistency. Not a single face swap, recapture, text patch, or
            hybrid got past. Four files defeated every native-resolution model I
            trained. Letterforms are the finest detail in the dataset, so they
            are the first thing to go when a card is squeezed to 224 pixels
            wide.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="project">
      <header class="role__head">
        <h3>LLM practicum grading system</h3>
        <p class="figure role__meta">
          Personal project, approved by the head of department · Python, Gemini
          API
        </p>
      </header>

      <ul class="role__points measure">
        <li>
          Reads the question, the answer key, and the lecturer's rubric, scores
          each submission against it, then writes an Excel recap with feedback
          per student. Covers eight sessions, six of material plus a quiz and a
          final.
        </li>
        <li>
          No retrieval layer. The whole context fits in one prompt, so RAG would
          have been machinery with nothing to do.
        </li>
        <li>
          Every output carries a confidence label. Anything below high
          confidence goes to a human before it counts.
        </li>
        <li>
          Answer keys drafted by the model are validated by the lecturer before
          they grade anything. Student code is read, never executed.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .project + .project {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    padding-top: 3.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .project__lede {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .pipeline {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 3px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .pipeline__step + .pipeline__step {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .pipeline summary {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.25rem minmax(0, 11rem) 1fr;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.35rem 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.95rem 1.1rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    transition: background var(--t-fast) var(--ease);
  }

  .pipeline summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .pipeline summary:hover {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--verified) 7%, var(--paper-raised));
  }

  @media (max-width: 44rem) {
    .pipeline summary {
      grid-template-columns: 2.25rem 1fr;
    }
    .pipeline__role {
      grid-column: 2;
    }
  }

  .pipeline__no {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .pipeline__stage {
    color: var(--verified);
    transition: letter-spacing var(--t-mid) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .pipeline details[open] .pipeline__stage {
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .pipeline__role {
    font-size: var(--size-caption);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .pipeline__detail {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 1.1rem 1.15rem calc(2.25rem + 1.85rem);
    font-size: var(--size-figure);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
  }

  @media (max-width: 44rem) {
    .pipeline__detail {
      padding-left: 1.1rem;
    }
  }

  /* Isi tahap yang dibuka meluncur turun, bukan muncul mendadak. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .pipeline details[open] .pipeline__detail {
      animation: slide-down var(--t-mid) var(--ease-out);
    }
  }

  @keyframes slide-down {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(-0.4rem);
    }
  }

  /* Satu-satunya tempat terakota dipakai di seluruh halaman.
     Bukan kartu membulat berpalang: sisipan bertepi lurus dengan garis
     terakota di atas dan label yang duduk di garis itu, seperti halaman
     catatan yang diselipkan ke dalam laporan. */
  .audit {
    position: relative;
    margin-top: 3.25rem;
    padding: 2rem 0 0;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--before-audit);
  }

  .audit__label {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    padding-right: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--before-audit);
    background: var(--paper);
  }

  .audit p + p {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
  }

  .audit__rest {
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
  }

  .audit__figure {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--size-figure);
    color: var(--before-audit);
  }

  /* Titik balik cerita. Satu kalimat yang membatalkan kecurigaan penulis
     sendiri, jadi diberi ruang seperti kutipan. */
  .audit__turn {
    max-width: 22ch;
    margin-block: 2rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.2rem + 1.4vw, 2.15rem);
    line-height: 1.22;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 40, "WONK" 1;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .audit code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
</style>
